  "reason": "Evidence: The current best config (config_013: multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.635) establishes that multiprofile + avgpool + weighted fusion is the strongest combination tested. However, the image encoder axis is completely untested — all 9 completed experiments use imagenet_vit_l. Uncertainty: We do not know whether the large ViT-L representation is essential or whether a ResNet50 backbone would perform comparably in the multimodal multiprofile setting. This question has high leverage: the answer determines whether ~15+ resnet50 configurations are worth pursuing or can be eliminated. Question tested: config_009 changes only the image encoder (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) relative to config_013, cleanly isolating the effect of image representation quality while holding RNA encoder, profile setting, aggregation, and fusion constant. Why this is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, resolving a binary, high-impact design axis (image encoder architecture) with a single-variable comparison is more informative than incremental tweaks to aggregation or RNA encoder, both of which already have partial evidence (avgpool > transformer; pca_n2000 >> scgpt in multiprofile). The result will either confirm imagenet_vit_l is necessary (focusing the search) or reveal resnet50 is competitive (opening a broader, potentially more efficient design space)."
}

